--+## Changed
--+
--+- `approve` now loads `osq.toml` before reading a change, decides whether git is on from `vcs.enabled` and the canonical repository root, and with git on approves into the change's own branch and worktree.
--+- Added the worktree orchestration: branch and worktree creation, `vcs.prepare`, rollback on prepare failure, recursive copy, `.run/approved`, `.run/base`, `.run/approver`, the approval commit, `worktree-add`/`worktree-prune`/`commit` tree records, stacked-copy removal, and checkout-draft removal.
--+- Added `osq-kernel-config`, `osq-kernel-harnesses`, and `osq-kernel-vcs` to the approve crate; `Cargo.lock` follows.
--+- Added `tests/approve_worktree.rs`, `tests/worktree_support/mod.rs`, and the copied `tests/fixtures/approve-worktree/` goldens.
--+- Made `reject::time` `pub(crate)` so the worktree record uses the existing UTC timestamp.
--+
--+## Deviated
--+
--+- `render` takes the change folder explicitly so tasks 3 and 4 can reuse the helper for other folders.
--+- Added a second git-off test whose scratch copy sits below a freshly initialized outer repository. It proves the root comparison even where `cargo-mutants`' source copy has no ambient `.git`, where the original git-off test alone cannot reach it.
--+
--+## Outside scope
--+
--+- `Cargo.lock` changed automatically when the new workspace dependencies were added; no task scopes it.
--+- While reproducing the mutation check locally with the root comparison forced true, one test run created a stray `osq/001-alpha-twice` branch and worktree entry in this checkout, now pointing at a removed scratch folder. Agents cannot run git to remove it; `git worktree prune` and `git branch -D osq/001-alpha-twice` in a human checkout would clear it (the branch holds one scratch approval commit).
--+
